{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The WiFi extender was the closest match because I have bought networking adapters, so its connection-related purpose felt relevant.",
    "That relevance was only partial: I would still skip it because I have no current need to extend WiFi coverage."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Smart speakers, streaming sticks and a smart plug serve entertainment or home automation needs that my computer accessory purchases do not suggest.",
    "Memory cards do not solve an identified need for me; buying adapters and cables does not mean I need removable storage.",
    "Different Echo generations and colors all miss for the same reason: I have no current use for a voice assistant."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations treated electronics as broadly interchangeable, although the practical purpose of each purchase matters to me.",
    "Several suggestions were much more popular than my past purchases, but widespread use does not give me a reason to choose them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My history points toward specific connection tasks, including adding USB ports, connecting a display and getting Ethernet access.",
    "My purchases are infrequent, and I need a concrete reason to buy another accessory rather than a loose connection to something I bought before.",
    "A recent Ethernet adapter purchase does not establish a WiFi coverage problem or a need for another networking device."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in electronics but mostly missed my focus on practical accessories for specific connection needs."
}"}
